    font: {fileID: 0}
    textSpeed: 0.024
    textPunctSpeed: 0.18
    lettersUntilSFX: 3
    sentences:
    - <SFX_liezel_concerned><i>(He speaks of salakab and the kapisanan as if they
      are the real enemy. What made him oppose them so strongly? Is he only blaming
      them to protect whatever the Disidensiya is planning?)</i>
    - <i>(Does he think salakab will eventually take over Giyala? How is that outcome
      any different from a government that drives its country to chaos in secret?)</i>
    - <SFX_liezel_frustrated>Is it not also inhumane to hide from the people one
      serves?
    - When the majority of people experience inexplicable events, one would rely
      on the highest models of governance...
    - "...and yet we gain no answers\u2014only more questions. There <i>must</i>
      be information that only a strong group of people would know of..."
